WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.810
Hey guys, I’m Abbey Sharp and welcome to
Abbey’s Kitchen.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:07.920
In today’s edition of What I Eat in a Day
Youtuber reviews, I will be taking a look

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.079
at Stephanie Joshi from the YouTube channel
Nutty Foodie Fitness.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:19.590
Stephanie is a model and fitness enthusiast
and is known for her WIEIAD videos and eating

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.590
challenges.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.970
Some examples of the food challenge videos
on her channel include the ever so popular

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:31.710
“10,000 calorie challenge”, “only eating
sweet food for 24 hours”, “eating peanut

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:37.210
butter for 24 hours” “eating nothing but
pizza for a day” … You get the gist.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:43.710
This also sounds eerily similar to our friend
Livia Adams from Always Hungry, but I am hoping

00:00:43.710 --> 00:01:08.280
we get a different narrative

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:14.070
from Stephanie.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:48.189
So, let’s meet Stephanie and take a look
at her first meals of

00:01:48.189 --> 00:02:03.909
the day.

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:09.950
Like the vast majority of us, Stephanie is
currently in self isolation and let’s just

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.390
say, the struggle is real.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:17.310
I can totally relate to the stress of not
finding the usual essential food items at

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:18.810
the store now a days.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:23.830
I would say that its more than a disappointment
when your go-to staples aren’t available,

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:29.860
for me, its actually stressful, especially
because I know I cant just pick it up somewhere

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.600
else so easily.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.450
Also, you guys need to know that I washed
my hair for you all today and Im now doing

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:41.821
that legit just once a week because I only
see you guys once a week ha.

00:02:41.821 --> 00:02:48.489
So yah, my hair, nails and skin better look
amazing after this is all done.

00:02:48.489 --> 00:03:03.800
let’s take a look at what she has for breakfast
on day one.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:09.370
What a gorgeous oatmeal bowl and I love the
apple pie flavour.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.959
I am a big fan of oats in the morning because
they are rich in carbs and fiber to help keep

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:16.019
you satiated.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:21.019
The specific fibre in oats beta glucan has
also been shown to help lower cholesterol

00:03:21.019 --> 00:03:26.580
which is probably not an issue for stephanie,
but is a really huge selling point for a lot

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.190
of other adults.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:34.379
One thing we need to be mindful of is balancing
it out with a source of protein, especially

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:35.379
at breakfast.

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:40.080
That would usually come from the milk that’s
added to the oats, but since Stephanie is

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.769
using a milk alternative like oat milk, the
protein content is kind of lacking here.

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:51.870
So even though we have a good amount of carbs
from the oats, apple, and granola, and also

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.630
some healthy fats from the chia seed, I would
love to see a little extra protein from nut

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:04.300
butter, protein powder, Greek yogurt, or a
little more chia or hemp on top, or an egg

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:33.260
or two on 
the side.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:39.150
Okay so here we are seeing Stephanie eating
a substantially larger breakfast than she

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.729
did on day 1.

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:46.909
She mentions having already eaten oats for
breakfast (4:44), then has a bite of her friend’s

00:04:46.909 --> 00:04:52.599
leftover scrambled eggs, two pieces of toast
with smoked salmon, egg, and avocado, and

00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:53.599
two pancakes.

00:04:53.599 --> 00:04:59.610
It’s a lot of food, but I mean, we can all
relate to the hotel brunch effect I will call

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.610
it.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:05.369
It’s actually quite normal to eat more than
you may normally while travelling, partially

00:05:05.369 --> 00:05:11.080
because you may be walking more, have more
food options available to you, or you’re

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.740
just influenced by the eating patterns of
others around you.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.520
Having said that, it still does feel like
a lot of food at once in comparison to her

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:20.789
day 1 breakfast.

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:26.479
Now we are still learning about Stephanie,
so I don’t know if she just has a normal

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:34.419
hearty appetite, or if this is like a cheat
day / eating challenge situation.

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:38.740
A lot of people who are stuck in diet culture,
find that having a big “cheat meal like

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:44.169
breakfast” can kinda set them up for a binge
the rest of the day.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:48.460
It’s kinda like the “oh I just blew my
diet, might as well continue down this course

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:51.559
for the rest of the day and then tighten the
reigns tomorrow.”

00:05:51.559 --> 00:05:55.840
So I’m interested to see how the rest of
that day unfolds.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:13.020
But first, breakfast 3.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:19.309
Okay so this oatmeal breakfast looks great
and is my favourite of the three– we’ve

00:06:19.309 --> 00:06:25.029
got healthy carbs from the oats and banana,
protein from the salted caramel protein powder

00:06:25.029 --> 00:06:28.649
and some peanut butter for healthy fats.

00:06:28.649 --> 00:06:35.099
So this would be a more balanced option than
her day 1 oatmeal bowl, but just as delicious.

00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:41.119
She also added in some toffee flavoured drops,which
have no calories, sugar or fat.

00:06:41.119 --> 00:06:45.870
Theyre basically just a sweetener made with
sucralose which is like Splenda along with

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:49.429
some natural flavours and caramel colour syrup.

00:06:49.429 --> 00:06:53.520
So that’s a fine add in if you want to cut
back on sugar.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:59.490
but if you haven’t watched my video on artificial
sweeteners, check it out right here.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:23.719
Let’s see whats next.

00:07:23.719 --> 00:07:29.039
Okay so we clearly have a peanut butter lover
on our hands here which makes sense in the

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:31.430
context of her moniker.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:37.719
So after her oatmeal breakfast, Stephanie
is having a little apple with 20 spoonfuls

00:07:37.719 --> 00:07:40.899
of peanut butter as a mid-morning snack.

00:07:40.899 --> 00:07:48.089
Now, I love the combination of apples and
nut butter because we have fibre, protein

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:55.389
and healthy fat, but the ratio of apple to
nut butter is a little off.

00:07:55.389 --> 00:08:01.949
Nut butter is really energy dense so it’s
very easy to eat a large amount of calories

00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:07.580
in a small package, which is amazing for those
trying to gain weight or bulk up.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:12.050
And as Stephanie sort of mentions later on
in her videos, she does refer to going to

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:16.300
the gym to “make gains”, so this may be
the case for her.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:22.550
But for most people, 1 or 2 tablespoons would
be sufficient for a balanced snack and 20

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:25.229
tablespoons might look a bit like a binge.

00:08:25.229 --> 00:08:31.330
Again, im still getting to know her style
so obviously I’m not making any assumptions.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:36.440
She does however mention that she has 4 different
jars of peanut butter beside her bed, which

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.560
may be triggering for some people.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:43.589
I always recommend keeping food in the kitchen
or pantry, and actually putting your food

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:51.040
in a bowl or plate to eat out of, rather than
mindlessly snacking out of a jar or big bag.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.709
If you’re still hungry after you finish
the food in your bowl, by all means, go get

00:08:55.709 --> 00:09:01.769
more, but but eating food in a more purposeful
way just helps you get more in tune with your

00:09:01.769 --> 00:09:06.639
hunger and fullness cues as you move through
your intuitive eating journey.

00:09:06.639 --> 00:09:21.569
Lets

00:09:21.569 --> 00:09:33.310
take a look at lunch.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:38.360
So Stephanie mentions a few supplements she
has, not sure if shes necessarily taking them

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.500
or just that shes promoting them as an affiliate,
but a few things to note on this.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.420
One, a reminder to influencers to disclose
your partnerships at the top of the video,

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.380
I think ive said enough about that.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.800
And two, let’s talk about hair strengthening
supplements.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:10:00.690
Now I have NO clue whats in this particular
gummy because she doesn’t say, but speaking

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:05.480
from a nutrition perspective – there are
several vitamins and minerals that certainly

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:11.329
play a role in hair growth and strengthening
including Vitamin A, B Vitamins, Vitamin C,

00:10:11.329 --> 00:10:14.529
Vitamin D, Vitamin D, Iron, Zinc, and Protein.

00:10:14.529 --> 00:10:20.779
However, its important to note that these
natural supplements are not well regulated

00:10:20.779 --> 00:10:24.339
meaning that many of them are not approved
by the FDA.

00:10:24.339 --> 00:10:30.279
So theres no real research to prove whether
or not certain supplements, like a hair supplement,

00:10:30.279 --> 00:10:37.009
even work, and the claims a lot of these companies
make are off base.

00:10:37.009 --> 00:10:43.569
So I’m not suggesting that they don’t
work, they might help, but having a balanced

00:10:43.569 --> 00:11:12.509
healthy diet and good hair genes – which
she clearly does - is also key.

00:11:12.509 --> 00:11:17.690
Okay so before her breakfast, she did a little
mini workout in her kitchen doing some push

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:25.130
ups, and then shortly after we’re seeing
a classic English Breakfast with bacon, eggs,

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:30.000
garlic mushrooms, tomatoes, noodles, a bagel
and baked beans.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.550
I didn’t know the brits had noodles for
breakfast- but my british fans, is that common?

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:38.360
I want to know!

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:41.040
Anyway, lots going on here.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:48.470
We got protein from the baked beans, bacon,
and eggs; some veggie action with the tomato

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:54.140
and mushroom; carbs from the bagel and noodles.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:58.680
She is also not afraid to add fat to her meal
as she coated the frying pan with butter,

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:03.850
which is refreshing to see, given the “no
oil trend” is so rampant in the wellness

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:05.079
community.

00:12:05.079 --> 00:12:11.360
But if she wanted to balance out the higher
amounts of saturated fat from the bacon, eggs

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:17.240
and butter, she could have opted for an unsaturated
fat like olive oil for cooking in.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:23.710
It’s a hearty meal and definitely one that
is higher in animal fat and more refined carbs

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:29.829
than I would want to recommend regularly,
but we are living in unusual times right now,

00:12:29.829 --> 00:12:34.620
so its normal for your eating patterns to
be unusual.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:41.180
A lot of us are turning to more comfort foods
while in isolation and that is totally normal

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:45.759
– ive talked about that extensively here.

00:12:45.759 --> 00:12:50.050
So I’m totally okay with these kinds of
meals in moderation, especially in the context

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:56.560
of stephanie’s day because she had a low
fat, low protein breakfast with the oats.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:05.939
Let’s take a look at day 2.

00:13:05.939 --> 00:13:20.079
Haha okay that guy knows where its at – chocolate
orange combo is the WORST.

00:13:20.079 --> 00:13:25.519
Like this video if you agree haha just kidding.

00:13:25.519 --> 00:13:33.990
Okay so after their epic hotel brunch, she’s
doing a tour of a protein powder factory,

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:37.779
the one that I guess shes an affiliate for
(but doesn’t really properly disclose).

00:13:37.779 --> 00:13:43.100
So it makes sense now that she wanted to have
a larger meal because she was going to be

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.160
out and about before she could eat again.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:51.529
I mean, this is super typical for travel days
so I’m glad she was able to anticipate her

00:13:51.529 --> 00:13:56.720
day and plan her eating accordingly – though
it does look like she was at least able to

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:14.550
sample some of the protein drinks as

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:24.749
a little snack.

00:14:24.749 --> 00:14:30.339
Now stephanie is on the way to the gym with
her friends and we see that she has a BCAA

00:14:30.339 --> 00:14:35.410
beverage and some truffle chocolates, which
were later followed up with a fruit smoothie.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:39.139
This actually looks like a pretty good pre-workout
snack.

00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:44.480
We are getting some fast digesting carbs from
the fruit smoothie which you want to have

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:50.589
prior to a workout to give you energy, and
also a BCAA beverage.

00:14:50.589 --> 00:14:56.249
BCAA’s stand for Branched Chain Amino Acids
and they are commonly taken as a supplement

00:14:56.249 --> 00:15:02.430
containing 3 essential amino acids leucine,
isoleucine and valine.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:07.019
While there is some research that BCAAs may
aid in muscle soreness and fatigue and muscle

00:15:07.019 --> 00:15:12.680
mass, most research does not suggest this
is superior to getting a complete source of

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:18.309
protein with all 9 essential amino acids from
more cost effective food or a supplement like

00:15:18.309 --> 00:15:19.790
whey protein.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:25.351
So by all means, take BCAAs to support your
workout if you find they work for you, but

00:15:25.351 --> 00:15:31.100
you can also get adequte amounts in your diet
from foods like tofu, beans, meat, poultry,

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:37.870
fish, eggs, pumpkin seeds, and quinoa.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:50.189
Okay so not surprisingly given Stephanies
larger than normal breakfast, she doesn’t

00:15:50.189 --> 00:15:56.889
have a full lunch this day, just the supplements
and smoothie which is probably because she’s

00:15:56.889 --> 00:16:01.930
not that full.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:09.850
I’m glad she got a little fuel in the tank
pre-workout and that she was just listening

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:14.709
to her body’s needs rather than pulling
a typical cheat day stunt where she started

00:16:14.709 --> 00:16:19.290
the day off with a larger than normal meal,
and then said oh screw it, I guess I will

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:24.770
just eat everything I can.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:33.470
Lets take a look at day 3.

00:16:33.470 --> 00:17:00.589
Oh my god, where is this restaurant?

00:17:00.589 --> 00:17:06.069
The food looks amazing and almost too pretty
to eat.

00:17:06.069 --> 00:17:10.770
But also I think this girl legit ordered everything
in the menu, and it looks like she does a

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:17.140
pretty good job of polishing it off- down
to the balsamic glaze on her plate.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:22.309
We got the layered smoothie, pancakes, avocado
toast on a waffle, a chicken sandwich with

00:17:22.309 --> 00:17:27.089
salad, cheese tortellini, AND a pistachio
donut.

00:17:27.089 --> 00:17:31.450
That is a total of 5 full lunch entrees AND
a dessert.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:37.210
It’s hard to know if she’s shared everything
or not, but regardless, it’s a large amount

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:46.010
of food, so I am a bit concerned this is teetering
in eating challenge/ cheat day territory.

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:57.870
Lets check out her snacks.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:03.490
So after a carb heavy breakfast, a fat and
protein heavy lunch, we’re back for a sweet

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:14.419
treat here for afternoon tea.

00:18:14.419 --> 00:18:23.940
Wow.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:29.450
Okay so this matcha chia pudding-like concoction
that Stephanie made for her snack is pretty

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:30.780
genius, I have to say.

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:37.480
Though it does have a dessert-like feel with
the matcha kit kat, its still pretty nutrient

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:38.480
dense.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:43.320
We have some protein from the protein powder
and yogurt, healthy fats from the chia seed

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:48.990
and peanut butter, and carbs from the banana
and granola.

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:55.260
I will say in combination with the two cake
slices she just had, we are definitely racking

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.399
up the added sugar.

00:18:57.399 --> 00:19:05.450
So far we’re at roughly 150 g of sugar this
day, and we still have meals to come.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:12.841
Now day 2, which was her restaurant travel
day, she doesn’t have another snack, so

00:19:12.841 --> 00:19:34.830
let’s move along to

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:45.990
day 3.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:20:01.250
So, based on this short little clip it appears
that Stephanie eats spoonful’s of peanut

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.899
butter as her pre-workout snack.

00:20:03.899 --> 00:20:10.059
Though we don’t see how many she has exactly,
she is also coming off the heels of her massive

00:20:10.059 --> 00:20:15.100
brunch meal so I imagine she must still be
feeling pretty full from that.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:20.500
But also, this is also the same day that she
had 20 spoonful’s of peanut butter, so I

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:26.700
really can’t be sure where her relationship
with food and her appetite is that day.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:32.380
From a more practical nutrition science stand
point, straight up peanut butter is not the

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:34.610
best preworkout snack.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:39.669
The fat slows down the rate of digestion,
and it doesn’t deliver the fast acting carbs

00:20:39.669 --> 00:20:42.360
that we need to perform.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:47.760
Ideally we want to have the majority of the
fat in our day spaced out away from our workouts,

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:53.890
so maybe if she was hungry before she trained,
a combination of carbs and protein would have

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.620
been a better choice.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:21:00.570
Exact amounts would depend on the length of
time between when she ate and when she hit

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:01.570
the gym.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:06.690
But if lets say Stephanie ate 30 minutes before
her workout, she would want to aim for about

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:13.380
10-20 grams of carbs, which might look like
one banana or one fruit, either on their own

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:18.090
or with some Greek yogurt for protein to boost
the satiety factor.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:27.090
Lets see what dinner has in store.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:36.899
Yes, I LOVE this.

00:21:36.899 --> 00:21:42.649
I love slow cooker meals like this, and this
looks perfectly balanced.

00:21:42.649 --> 00:21:48.430
We got some protein from the chicken, carbs
from the potato, and of course a ton of bright

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:50.260
and colourful veggies.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:56.700
I’m happy to see that after a sugar heavy
snack on this day, we’ve got a really nutrient

00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:02.890
dense meal to end the day.

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:19.390
Okay so

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:25.850
for most people who have had a hearty brunch
with lots of carbs and fat, I would say yah,

00:22:25.850 --> 00:22:28.890
this dinner totally makes sense.

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:34.669
We have satiating protein and fat from the
steak and edamame, and lots of veg with the

00:22:34.669 --> 00:22:35.799
rapini.

00:22:35.799 --> 00:22:40.350
But considering she just completed a pretty
heavy duty workout, I would have liked to

00:22:40.350 --> 00:22:44.940
see some carbs to replenish glycogen stores.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:55.450
Lets take a look at day 3.. this one meal
might tell us

00:22:55.450 --> 00:23:01.330
a lot.

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:17.769
Hm ... yah, this is kinda what I was afraid
of with stephanie’s day 3.

00:23:17.769 --> 00:23:26.220
So we have chicken wings, chicken strips,
coleslaw, coke, ice cream, cookies, and a

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:29.240
few different pizzas.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:35.590
This scene is playing out exactly like any
mukbang or cheat day challenge, and in the

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:42.450
context of her day with a big oatmeal breakfast,
peanut butter, huge brunch, more peanut butter,

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:49.210
and now, all of this – it is definitely
feeling potentially problematic.

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:54.070
At one point even her friend comments on how
much she’s eaten.

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:58.860
I get that she’s trying to make “gains”
but there are definitely more nourishing ways

00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:04.890
to go about that that will satisfy her nutritional
needs without an excessive amount of saturated

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:07.970
fat, salt and sugar.

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:15.130
Now I am all for ordering in occasionally,
and pizza night is a Friday night tradition

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:24.010
in my house, but shes just consumed 90 grams
of saturated fat and 15,800 mg of sodium in

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:26.520
this one meal alone.

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:32.210
That is 10 times more than the recommended
amount of sodium and 7 times the amount of

00:24:32.210 --> 00:24:35.770
saturated fat for the day.

00:24:35.770 --> 00:24:40.880
Consuming that much sodium in one sitting
has the potential to not only cause bloating,

00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:44.800
and over time, significantly increase blood
pressure.

00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:51.179
Basically, a diet that is consistently high
in sodium can injure blood vessel walls, contributing

00:24:51.179 --> 00:24:53.149
to plaque build up.

00:24:53.149 --> 00:25:00.029
This blocks blood flow which makes the heart
work harder to pump blood throughout the body,

00:25:00.029 --> 00:25:03.220
increasing the risk of heart attack, stroke,
and heart failure.

00:25:03.220 --> 00:25:10.130
When it comes to saturated fat and heart health,
the research is mixed as this is a bit of

00:25:10.130 --> 00:25:12.350
a controversial topic.

00:25:12.350 --> 00:25:16.809
The relationship between saturated fat and
heart disease is not 100% clear.

00:25:16.809 --> 00:25:22.280
BUT, dietary guidelines do continue to suggest
limiting saturated fat in the diet because

00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:25.850
it MAY have negative implications for heart
health.

00:25:25.850 --> 00:25:42.909
But regardless, I cannot speak for Stephanie,
but consuming 7 times the amount of saturated

00:25:42.909 --> 00:25:48.010
fat in one sitting cant possibly feel good
for most people.

00:25:48.010 --> 00:25:59.320
Okay so let’s finish things off with dessert.

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:06.669
So clearly stephanie is a matcha fan, and
those look like cute little treats.

00:26:06.669 --> 00:26:11.279
Now while matcha may help have some brain
and heart health benefits, one thing to keep

00:26:11.279 --> 00:26:21.019
in mind is it has greater amount of caffeine
than green tea, so it might not be great idea

00:26:21.019 --> 00:26:22.850
to have them before bed.

00:26:22.850 --> 00:26:29.000
I also feel like shes had a sugar heavy day
this day as is, so if she were hungry before

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:35.809
bed, maybe something like cottage cheese or
yogurt with some fresh fruit would have been

00:26:35.809 --> 00:27:02.299
a more balanced choice.

00:27:02.299 --> 00:27:07.669
Okay so now I know that If we are to ever
go out to eat with Stephanie that we cannot

00:27:07.669 --> 00:27:13.929
leave our food unattended ha, but okay so
that looks delish.

00:27:13.929 --> 00:27:21.530
I guess it’s a good thing we’re getting
some carbs with that dinner after the workout,

00:27:21.530 --> 00:27:27.630
but would have been ideal to get more complex
carbs so that she doesn’t get a sugar crash

00:27:27.630 --> 00:27:31.559
in the night.

00:27:31.559 --> 00:27:37.230
While you may feel sleepy after a carb heavy
meal aka a carb coma, research suggests that

00:27:37.230 --> 00:27:42.840
sugar can interfere with deep sleep, which
will leave you feeling less rested the next

00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:48.020
day.

00:27:48.020 --> 00:27:52.300
Lets see day 3.

00:27:52.300 --> 00:28:40.139
Okay, so its very clear to

00:28:40.139 --> 00:29:09.730
me here that we have a lot more going on that
maybe we don’t see on stephanie’s channel.

00:29:09.730 --> 00:29:17.691
It’s possible we’re dealing with the “extreme
hunger” weve heard other influencers talk

00:29:17.691 --> 00:29:23.380
about like stephanie buttermore or always
hungry, as these meals and days look very

00:29:23.380 --> 00:29:26.610
much the same.

00:29:26.610 --> 00:29:34.159
Okay so let me give you my overall thoughts
on this series of what I eat in a day.

00:29:34.159 --> 00:29:36.620
in general, is this way of eating balanced?

00:29:36.620 --> 00:29:42.940
I am having a lot of mixed feelings watching
a lot of Stephanie’s videos and having a

00:29:42.940 --> 00:29:44.389
hard time reading them.

00:29:44.389 --> 00:29:49.240
On the one hand, I love her enthusiasm for
food.

00:29:49.240 --> 00:29:56.370
I also just love watching her because I think
shes got a real vibrant energy and is super

00:29:56.370 --> 00:29:58.200
cute and sweet.

00:29:58.200 --> 00:30:03.889
She also made a specific disclaimer in her
day 3 video about it not being a cheat day,

00:30:03.889 --> 00:30:04.889
take a look.

00:30:04.889 --> 00:30:07.659
So I love this philosophy and share it wholeheartedly.

00:30:07.659 --> 00:30:34.139
So I think it’s great that this day

00:30:34.139 --> 00:31:22.090
of

00:31:22.090 --> 00:31:28.070
eating isn’t a special day, and that she
isn’t going to then restrict heavily the

00:31:28.070 --> 00:31:29.850
next day.

00:31:29.850 --> 00:32:50.340
She also addresses peoples assumptions

00:32:50.340 --> 00:33:49.450
that she’s bulimic.

00:33:49.450 --> 00:33:56.379
Okay so here we see Stephanie talk about how
her appetite has always been larger than average,and

00:33:56.379 --> 00:34:02.039
that no two people’s nutritional needs are
the same so not to compare.

00:34:02.039 --> 00:34:06.929
That’s true and that’s a really important
message to share.

00:34:06.929 --> 00:34:12.960
None of this means stephanie has an eating
disorder, or that she is necessarily restricting,

00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:15.150
or that she is throwing up her food.

00:34:15.150 --> 00:34:17.830
None of that is the necessary truth.

00:34:17.830 --> 00:34:20.540
We don’t know that, I don’t know that.

00:34:20.540 --> 00:34:28.280
I am admittedly just a bit troubled by what
to say here because the reality is, I don’t

00:34:28.280 --> 00:34:30.470
know everything about stephanie.

00:34:30.470 --> 00:34:37.940
All I see are the videos she posts but from
what I do see, I do have some concerns., Her

00:34:37.940 --> 00:34:45.020
experience does remind me of stephanie buttermore’s
“extreme hunger” as she went through her

00:34:45.020 --> 00:34:46.360
All In Journey.

00:34:46.360 --> 00:34:51.780
But what we saw with Stephanie Buttermore’s
experience, was extreme hunger as a result

00:34:51.780 --> 00:34:58.920
of extreme calorie restriction which totally
altered her hunger and satiety hormones and

00:34:58.920 --> 00:35:02.060
actually damaged a number of biological functions.

00:35:02.060 --> 00:35:07.560
It’s actually true that in these circumstances
– that is, when you have a history of restriction

00:35:07.560 --> 00:35:14.740
and associated low body fat, the body may
actually need a drastic amount of calories

00:35:14.740 --> 00:35:22.320
to provide basic nutrition for basic daily
needs PLUS extra to repair the damage.

00:35:22.320 --> 00:35:27.540
What can happen is that your enteric nervous
system (that is the reflex circuits in your

00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:33.250
gut) is receiving information that you’re
physically full, yet the central nervous system

00:35:33.250 --> 00:35:38.890
(aka your brain) is receiving information
that more energy is required to return to

00:35:38.890 --> 00:35:41.880
a balanced state.

00:35:41.880 --> 00:35:52.920
The drive to eat a lot of calories- even 10,000
calories, is very normal in this circumstance,

00:35:52.920 --> 00:35:59.570
and should be honoured as its all about energy
restoration or building back what is maybe

00:35:59.570 --> 00:36:01.900
not working optimally.

00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:08.490
There is good evidence to support this process,
as crazy as it may sound, so I’ll link to

00:36:08.490 --> 00:36:10.850
some really good resources below.

00:36:10.850 --> 00:36:15.480
Now I want to reiterate that I do not know
if this stephanie is restricting on the days

00:36:15.480 --> 00:36:22.370
she isn’t showing on her channel like buttermore
did, but I just wanted to share that information

00:36:22.370 --> 00:36:27.050
on what we know about extreme hunger in general.

00:36:27.050 --> 00:36:35.510
What I can say is that between these three
what I eat in a day videos, nevermind the

00:36:35.510 --> 00:36:42.110
official eating challenges she puts up, there
is a huge range in caloric consumption.

00:36:42.110 --> 00:36:49.320
According to our calculations, Stephanie consumed
3000 calories on day 1, 1750 calories on day

00:36:49.320 --> 00:36:54.870
2, and a total of 11, 430 calories on day
3.

00:36:54.870 --> 00:36:57.040
That’s quite the range, my friends.

00:36:57.040 --> 00:37:01.570
And after taking a look at her macros, her
fat intake is either on the higher end of

00:37:01.570 --> 00:37:07.990
the 20-35% total calorie recommendation or
totally surpasses it.

00:37:07.990 --> 00:37:14.640
Now it’s normal- very very normal- for us
not to eat the same amount of calories each

00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:15.640
day.

00:37:15.640 --> 00:37:18.350
But these discrepancies are pretty extreme.

00:37:18.350 --> 00:37:25.770
One study suggested that that average daily
caloric variability for women would be + or

00:37:25.770 --> 00:37:32.450
- 25% of their total energy needs.. which
would mean that Stephanie caloric intake would

00:37:32.450 --> 00:37:38.410
ideally sit within a 1650 – 2750 caloric
range.

00:37:38.410 --> 00:37:44.920
but from these three videos, only one of Stephanies
WIEIAD’s is within this range and I assume

00:37:44.920 --> 00:37:49.660
if we were to also factor in a lot of her
other eating challenge videos, we would see

00:37:49.660 --> 00:37:51.950
even greater discrepancy.

00:37:51.950 --> 00:37:57.660
Also, even if Stephanie is in a bulk phase,
which I’m just speculating by her use of

00:37:57.660 --> 00:38:04.990
hashtags like #gains on her instagram, her
day 3 contains substantially more food than

00:38:04.990 --> 00:38:09.900
what we would typically see in even a man’s
bulk phase.

00:38:09.900 --> 00:38:15.130
Again, everyone’s normal needs are super
unique, but I’m just speaking to patterns

00:38:15.130 --> 00:38:16.850
and averages I see.

00:38:16.850 --> 00:38:21.800
I would also say that even if this variability
is normal for her, and is not the result of

00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:27.910
“extreme hunger” or previous restriction,
which they very well may be, again, I cant

00:38:27.910 --> 00:38:34.210
deny her that legitimate possibility, I would
have liked to see her meet those needs in

00:38:34.210 --> 00:38:37.190
a more balanced way.

00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:43.920
Sugar, salt and saturated fat are all fine
in moderation, but there are days she’s

00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:49.300
getting 10x the amount of sodium, 16 x the
amount of saturated fat, and 6 x the amount

00:38:49.300 --> 00:38:51.860
of sugar to meet her needs.

00:38:51.860 --> 00:38:56.920
Like we mentioned, excessive intake of sodium
is linked to bloating, and high blood pressure

00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:59.070
which can put one at risk for heart disease.

00:38:59.070 --> 00:39:03.680
Too much sugar can likewise increase the risk
of heart disease and can also lead to increased

00:39:03.680 --> 00:39:05.110
risk of developing type 2 diabetes, weight
gain, acne, and cancer..…..

00:39:05.110 --> 00:39:09.980
Especially if shes going to continue with
these eating challenges which are even more

00:39:09.980 --> 00:39:16.060
extreme, I would just want to be mindful of
her usual diet.

00:39:16.060 --> 00:39:21.140
Now, are there any problematic claims or assumptions
made by this channel?

00:39:21.140 --> 00:39:26.180
So I actually really like stephanie’s attitude
towards food.

00:39:26.180 --> 00:39:31.350
We do not see Stephanie using any diet-y language
whatsoever.

00:39:31.350 --> 00:39:39.050
She also does not seem to be overly preoccupied
with her weight, or what she eats, or how

00:39:39.050 --> 00:39:41.140
much, which I like.

00:39:41.140 --> 00:39:48.160
I would just flag that again, some of her
content may be triggering for a lot of people

00:39:48.160 --> 00:39:54.290
who struggle in their relationship with food
because her behaviours can read as problematic,

00:39:54.290 --> 00:39:58.750
even if they aren’t actually for her, if
that makes sense.

00:39:58.750 --> 00:40:02.010
Finally, what can we take away from Stephanie’s
channel?

00:40:02.010 --> 00:40:07.780
I would say the biggest take away for me is
stephanies glowing and fun personality.

00:40:07.780 --> 00:40:13.870
I love that she loves food, and for me, she
herself is really a pleasure to watch, even

00:40:13.870 --> 00:40:19.260
if I sometime find her meal schemes hard to
enjoy.

00:40:19.260 --> 00:40:20.260
Bottom Line

00:40:20.260 --> 00:40:25.550
Though I do appreciate Stephanie’s enthusiasm
and openness with food, I do worry about how

00:40:25.550 --> 00:40:30.390
this may be interpreted by her viewers who
may have struggled or are currently struggling

00:40:30.390 --> 00:40:33.490
with disordered eating or an eating disorder.

00:40:33.490 --> 00:40:38.580
It is totally healthy and balanced to enjoy
pizza or a matcha flavoured donut from time

00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:39.580
to time.

00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:44.170
It’s also okay to occasionally eat a lof
ot peanut butter off the spoon.

00:40:44.170 --> 00:40:50.790
But taken together with the plethora of extreme
eating challenges, insatiable hunger, and

00:40:50.790 --> 00:40:57.010
strange nut butter rituals, I just worry about
how it will all be interpreted by vulnerable

00:40:57.010 --> 00:40:58.010
viewers.

00:40:58.010 --> 00:41:02.720
I also think there are definitely much more
balanced ways to get your calories in – even

00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:08.840
if they are extreme- that don’t look like
multiple pizzas, ice cream, and wings in one

00:41:08.840 --> 00:41:09.840
sitting.

00:41:09.840 --> 00:41:13.710
While I do think Stephanie is trying to set
a good example for her followers by demonstrating

00:41:13.710 --> 00:41:18.120
that you don’t need to be afraid of food,
and you can enjoy food without being overly

00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:23.680
preoccupied with weight or wrapped up in diet
culture, I would have liked to see her communicate

00:41:23.680 --> 00:41:28.260
this message physically in a more balanced
and consistent way.

00:41:28.260 --> 00:41:33.680
I want to conclude by reminding you all to
be kind in the comments, both to me and to

00:41:33.680 --> 00:41:36.290
Stephanie if you do choose to reach out.

00:41:36.290 --> 00:41:41.110
We need to work to support people through
their eating journeys, not to tear them down

00:41:41.110 --> 00:41:44.460
and criticize them for being “wrong”.

00:41:44.460 --> 00:41:49.910
There is no right or wrong in this situation,
we’re all just using our own unique set

00:41:49.910 --> 00:41:52.240
of coping strategies to get by.

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:55.320
and on that note, that all for this today’s
video.

